        "math:completing-square-expression",
        "cnm_235"
      ],
      "explanation": "The fixed sum lets us express the product using one variable: \\(y=1-x\\). Completing the square then reveals a bound:\n\\[\nxy=x(1-x)=\\frac14-\\left(x-\\frac12\\right)^2.\n\\]\nFor every real \\(x\\), the squared term is nonnegative, so \\(xy\\leq\\tfrac14\\). Equality is possible: taking \\(x=y=\\tfrac12\\) satisfies \\(x+y=1\\) and gives \\(xy=\\tfrac14\\). Thus the largest value is \\(\\boxed{0.25}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
